747fe547b12b8b58c4a8c92a109586619077545d16c1340e0d496f948f258eab","note:permission-view:1c9f35e492634361b96cb50f0ca73d2196b4e1859c1576394b5d67befa24752f","note:permission-view:d0b6bd549d8924e123183ce9a499f26ea477a9dfdf48484ef026c3be13be0cd7","note:permission-view:7b4bc2854791c3773ff1a8c895ebed3ef8a351dec0736876c11a77c437b32414","note:permission-view:aec8aec58c7ac9d277c0705de1303271574c70b392d65c6fe73c67da8575278f"],"processing":{"active_assignments":14,"authorization_diagnoses":{},"binding_decisions":438,"bound_candidates":45,"excluded_binding_decisions":360,"extraction_complete":true,"extraction_receipts":54,"failure_holds":0,"incomplete_extractions":0,"live_candidates":53,"no_assignment_decisions":0,"pending_binding_reviews":38,"rejected_relationships":0,"scoped_control_holds":0,"semantic_stages":{"combined_incremental":{"calls":54,"elapsed_s":243.24941850733012},"incremental_repair":{"calls":42,"elapsed_s":251.09617100004107}},"source_events":54},"query_scope":"authenticated-requester-only"},"output":{"action":"answer","answer":"For pain, use acetaminophen 650 mg every 6 hours as needed (maximum 3,000 mg per day). For nausea, start doxylamine 12.5 mg nightly and pyridoxine 25 mg twice daily. You should stop ibuprofen.","answer_structured":{"medication_to_stop":"Ibuprofen","nausea_medication":"Doxylamine 12.5 mg nightly and Pyridoxine 25 mg BID","pain_medication":"Acetaminophen 650 mg q6h PRN (max 3,000 mg/day)"},"retrieved_memory":[{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:fd774520ca5c8449ab4373a7aabe4c18ea08fe328849b18db247c7727d93f2de","text":"Medication plan after initial clinician review: stop ibuprofen; use acetaminophen 650 mg q6h PRN with 3,000 mg/day max; continue prenatal vitamin and levothyroxine 75 mcg daily; start doxylamine 12.5 mg nightly and pyridoxine 25 mg BID."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:9cf3ee92af3d8557c88f178f7889ee1bd2d5880fbba26af749cea6ec8225375d","text":"Mostly morning nausea, no vomiting, but it has been getting more noticeable this week."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:0ea3f491775bec3fdc5f3dd0381a41f796f76874daeccf125ea7bd0840f26056","text":"Please keep the clinical details private."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:337430b0af0c79ed25438ec5c7af6f4dedabae78f75cd98580e3ee4174148c9f","text":"She can help me get to the appointments, but that's all."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:ae4ea0216a8c4e8a2975a27854fbbe252fbf19495d85fd0a1eb8c3228cecfdb1","text":"I can discuss logistical planning with you if Elena wants, but the clinical interpretation stays with Elena unless she changes that instruction."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:ef272c8dbc467239cb07b49db962c48da5b5dbc3f2b000abc2440c4f08757b2b","text":"At this stage we often need serial labs and a follow-up scan before we can say whether the pregnancy is progressing normally."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:c61955214ba1f027c631ab43b90210b7f7823ae179f6fccb03ffcbcbdc7e26e4","text":"Let's review medications before Dr. Shah comes in."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:baedca4993ce101c1da650afe550226f4aeee575115d94ee5cc5ea24f504288e","text":"I'm taking a prenatal vitamin and levothyroxine 75 micrograms each morning."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:21020410065c989d6a855d59fffa7fe1763d8db8f0478299a6246ed1f473cd6e","text":"Triage note posted: bleeding light, pain 4/10, no syncope, no fever, no unilateral severe pain, sulfa rash allergy documented."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:177eaf2da94b09ca11434583335a201978a58fcad13cd6dee7ef4f5abd00a7ec","text":"Sulfa antibiotics give me a blotchy rash."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:60fa2e1e8869bcaffdebe8c1ceee52d7a8ac336df49a5e77ba4c78c8a768471a","text":"I had light bleeding and cramping."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:1720985455678c6b71bc81b31183c7807f4954c4fa37cce5457b60fdb97457ae","text":"No shoulder pain or fever."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:6ca4bc19c6f9d66a1f50e1e10988070f8ce8e897cd931a32e4d22153977eda51","text":"I'll keep the instruction narrow and operational: generic callback only, no pregnancy wording."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:d3d0f89eca946ab8c40444211cb0bee9510799f0f400af55feb2feb23c141f86","text":"Please keep the clinical parts between me and the care team."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:849fc2a5c20c94519cb1cdf4ceaf5441852cd2d82a3d61eb7e4326eb5824f5d1","text":"I share a family phone plan and I don't want anyone hearing a voicemail that mentions pregnancy or a scan."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:6e0dabe5aa63e460c00375c8a215e41a555278bca4f9381376ca54db7b61b4c1","text":"I'm drawing the ordered labs now: beta-hCG, CBC, type and screen, and a basic urine sample."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:4764fdb697607e59031aeaf433a5a97acca4f8e98350522d3c3931bfc51479d9","text":"She can hear appointment times and parking details for now, but not my results, medications, or notes."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:2b8b8d2c9e6c843a15410147a335a67d205be9f4be5df9f1bcb132aed150d60c","text":"The ED told me to come to the early pregnancy clinic because I've had spotting and cramping since last night."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:f8351ec80ae2664fef9766d8e8dcc0963c61392e18987b68265ac7ae9e5bb01d","text":"Mostly spotting."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:747fe547b12b8b58c4a8c92a109586619077545d16c1340e0d496f948f258eab","text":"The cramps are there, but they're not severe and they're on both sides."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:1c9f35e492634361b96cb50f0ca73d2196b4e1859c1576394b5d67befa24752f","text":"Done."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:d0b6bd549d8924e123183ce9a499f26ea477a9dfdf48484ef026c3be13be0cd7","text":"Please place the urine cup in the pass-through when you're ready."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:7b4bc2854791c3773ff1a8c895ebed3ef8a351dec0736876c11a77c437b32414","text":"I changed one liner this morning and one this afternoon."},{"memory_id":"note:permission-view:aec8aec58c7ac9d277c0705de1303271574c70b392d65c6fe73c67da8575278f","text":"My regular cell is 415-555-0122, but please do not use that number for pregnancy-related callbacks."}],"used_record_ids":["note:permission-view:fd774520ca5c8449ab4373a7aabe4c18ea08fe328849b18db247c7727d93f2de"]}}
